multiprofile-native (1.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Premium console redesign: the old single-file console (src/static/app.js)
    is replaced by a Next.js 15 / React 19 / TypeScript / Tailwind v4 static
    export served from the same src/static directory — no Node.js runtime
    needed on the machine. Hash routing, same Flask API contracts, all 33
    device presets with honest support badges, proxy fail-closed behaviour,
    and every existing backend feature preserved.
  * New 6-step New Profile wizard (Basic / Device / Network / Fingerprint /
    Consistency / Review) with proxy testing, device capability matrix, and
    local pre-flight checks; quick-create dialog kept with a "Full setup"
    cross-link.
  * Overview dashboard, Profiles table (filters, cursor pagination,
    selection, bulk actions, export with proxy passwords stripped),
    10-tab profile detail, Device Library, Fingerprint Inspector, Network
    (proxies/gateways/diagnostics), Jobs with live SSE updates, Audit log,
    and Settings (general, clients & templates, backups, extensions).
  * Global shell: command palette, keyboard shortcuts, light/dark/system
    themes, notifications, bearer-token dialog. Wizard code-split;
    first-load JS ~196 kB.
  * All seven version markers synchronized on 1.9.0.

