multiprofile-native (1.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Desktop logo: original Multiprofile mark (four isolated browser panes in
    a tight grid, pine teal #0e7c6b on deep ink #131a25) as SVG plus PNGs at
    512/256/128/64/48/32/16 installed under
    /usr/share/icons/hicolor/<size>/apps/multiprofile.png; the .desktop file
    now uses Icon=multiprofile (was utilities-terminal); postinst refreshes
    the icon cache when gtk-update-icon-cache exists. Same artwork drives
    src/static/app_icon.png, favicon.ico, the sidebar, the login card, and
    the pywebview window icon.
  * Light and dark mode: one Light/Dark segmented toggle in the console top
    bar, persisted with storeSet("mp_theme", ...); first launch follows
    prefers-color-scheme. data-theme is set on <html> before paint (no flash);
    Light keeps the current look, Dark restyles content surfaces with the
    existing --mp-* tokens. No new font, no purple accent.
  * Profile grid: explicit full-fill layouts for 1, 2, and 3 profiles — 1
    covers the whole work area; 2 side-by-side when wider than tall, else
    stacked; 3 as one row on wide displays, else a column (never a 2x2 with a
    blank cell). 4+ keep the current balanced grids. GridCalculator remains
    the tiling authority; CDP Browser.setWindowBounds applies; gap 0,
    margin 0, work-area clip unchanged. The grid is re-tiled after every
    launch and after every stop.
  * Stop stays stopped: stop_profile records an explicit user stop
    (STOPPING note), SIGTERMs, waits for the pid to die, then marks STOPPED,
    releases the slot, and re-tiles the survivors. The supervisor re-reads
    state before any restart and relaunches ONLY an unexpected exit from
    RUNNING — a user stop is never treated as a crash. Retries exhausted or
    a stop gone wrong park the profile in error; nothing relaunches until
    the user presses Launch.
  * All seven version markers synchronized on 1.8.0.

